pedic procedures; IFUSE TORQ, an additively-manufactured threaded implant designed to allow for osteointegration, or incorporation of the bone into the implant's porous surface and structure; IFUSE BEDROCK GRANITE, an implant with a machined titanium core and a tulip that attaches to the rod and provides fusion and fixation to the sacroiliac joint as a foundational element for segmental spinal fusion; and IFUSE TORQ TNT, a porous threaded design with lengths capable of spanning the posterior pelvis, passing through the ipsilateral ilium, sacrum, and through the contralateral ilium. The company markets its products primarily with a direct sales force, as well as through third-party sales agents and resellers. SI-BONE, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Laura A. Francis MBA | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 376 people. Revenue per employee of $534K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 20%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["SI-BONE, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.1B market cap on $201M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -110% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 87% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $9M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -8.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 731% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperformi